## Completion and direct review

Implemented a provider-neutral warm worker service loop that:
- performs bounded receives and processes one delivery at a time;
- exits without receiving when already draining;
- releases unstarted delivery when drain races with receipt;
- allows active execution to settle and prevents another receive;
- uses interruptible idle waits rather than busy-spinning;
- exposes stop reason and per-outcome processing counts;
- propagates receive failures with prior outcome context.

Validation:
- python -m behave tests/command_worker/features → 15 scenarios and 70 steps passed
- python -m pytest -q tests/command_worker plexus/cli/shared/command_tasks_test.py plexus/cli/shared/command_dispatch_test.py plexus/cli/shared/test_command_dispatch.py → 76 passed
- ruff check plexus/command_worker tests/command_worker → passed
- ruff format --check plexus/command_worker tests/command_worker → passed
- provider-boundary check → no forbidden imports

No Celery, dashboard, infrastructure, dependency, or provider code changed. Signal integration, task protection, cancellation, provider adapters, and deployment remain follow-up work.
